                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "00b779a6-b930-321a-85e4-dee30679d06e",
                        "entry_id": "f5dffee3-9b6c-3e54-86c0-65634e9015e7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui concerne les Cantons-de-l’Est ou leurs habitants ^([1])."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cb7639ab-0e16-318a-9b8f-fd0e352c3259",
                        "entry_id": "f5dffee3-9b6c-3e54-86c0-65634e9015e7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Relatif aux cantons."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b9d1fe8b-7bb9-40df-b1b4-060ad71b1ab9",
                                "sense_id": "cb7639ab-0e16-318a-9b8f-fd0e352c3259",
                                "text": "Il leur fut reproché leur vocation ruraliste d’un côté (et son incapacité à assimiler le fait urbain), et l’archaïsme des élus cantonniers de l’autre, notables peu représentatifs du corps social (hommes âgés et pour beaucoup élus dans le tissu rural) se comportant d’abord comme courtiers de leur territoire d’élection (difficulté à développer une vision départementale)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "1c4ad22b-c69f-304d-b667-3f5b751135cf",
                "word": "cantonnier",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "772f6481-11e5-450c-a0a5-0a99070ba6dd",
                        "entry_id": "1c4ad22b-c69f-304d-b667-3f5b751135cf",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "cantonniers"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "6846f273-fc2e-4e06-869b-61b2e3ef7c25",
                        "entry_id": "1c4ad22b-c69f-304d-b667-3f5b751135cf",
                        "tags": [
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "cantonnière"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4388ddd4-1c93-3bd2-a71b-8593eb6c85ef",
                        "entry_id": "1c4ad22b-c69f-304d-b667-3f5b751135cf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Celui qui est employé par l’administration pour travailler à l’entretien des routes."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Métier"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "794ccde9-09d5-4bd2-bcad-1682f2b86ef8",
                                "sense_id": "4388ddd4-1c93-3bd2-a71b-8593eb6c85ef",
                                "text": "Elle savait qu’après un herbage il y avait un poteau, ensuite un orme, une grange ou une cahute de cantonnier."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bb6ab53c-8184-4a48-8883-6637f744e324",
                                "sense_id": "4388ddd4-1c93-3bd2-a71b-8593eb6c85ef",
                                "text": "Autrefois, monsieur, il y avait à cette fontaine un seuil de pierre. Les cantonniers s’en sont servis comme de moellon pour la construction du pont qui est là-bas."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "67ddc6d2-5874-4863-a18a-16d8b9ad29d1",
                                "sense_id": "4388ddd4-1c93-3bd2-a71b-8593eb6c85ef",
                                "text": "Non seulement elle eût^([sic]) son renseignement, mais elle apprit qu’il avait exercé le métier de cantonnier et participé aux premiers gravillonnages des routes environnantes, jusqu’alors empierrées."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "81e9e802-3b4d-3ee8-af30-41fa00ff2e6f",
                        "entry_id": "1c4ad22b-c69f-304d-b667-3f5b751135cf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Balayeur."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "especially"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a268b3b7-9723-4e5a-a9cc-5f7ae06a0ccf",
                                "sense_id": "81e9e802-3b4d-3ee8-af30-41fa00ff2e6f",
                                "text": "Le balais^([sic]) est le grand classique du nettoyage d’une ville. […] Depuis quelques années, les cantonniers ont leur complément indispensable : le roule-sac dans lequel ils peuvent jeter les détritus, ramassés à la pelle, troisième accessoire du cantonnier."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "39d8b66b-d409-3306-a2fb-dc428dcd6ac7",
                        "entry_id": "1c4ad22b-c69f-304d-b667-3f5b751135cf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Préposé au maniement des sémaphores ferroviaires."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "66d3f0f9-589c-3b20-85c0-c6469864455c",
                        "entry_id": "1c4ad22b-c69f-304d-b667-3f5b751135cf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Fromage de Québec au lait de vache à pâte molle à croûte lavée."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Fromage"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3bff3d77-c538-455b-baa9-f772cd474ae0",
                        "source_entry_id": "1c4ad22b-c69f-304d-b667-3f5b751135cf",
                        "source_sense_description": "Ouvrier",
                        "target_lang_word": "roadman",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "roadman",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1c99daff-5fe8-3eb3-b1e2-2106961970da",
                                        "entry_id": "4ba40a11-ca83-3c47-bb97-2ccf4b98db10",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A man who builds or repairs roads."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fb44cfe8-f6d3-4868-9ff9-1231acdf9a0e",
                                                "sense_id": "1c99daff-5fe8-3eb3-b1e2-2106961970da",
                                                "text": "Ernest Tipping had known the road for over 35 years and seen the roadman repairing it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9db96b1b-fb2a-46f3-99a2-3800e81f84ec",
                                                "sense_id": "1c99daff-5fe8-3eb3-b1e2-2106961970da",
                                                "text": "Any reader turning to the original novel would hardly recognize it in the shadow of Hitchcock’s film, so preoccupied is it with describing the glens and heathery mountains of the Scottish highlands, inhabited with an unlikely cavalcade of native eccentrics: an innkeeper with literary aspirations, a Liberal candidate with pacifist sympathies, a lower-class roadman laid up by drink, a bald archaeologist who isn’t quite what he seems."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1d0f6589-077a-31b8-b35d-b63ec92129c8",
                                        "entry_id": "4ba40a11-ca83-3c47-bb97-2ccf4b98db10",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A member of a subculture characterised by their clothing (notably puffer jackets and sportswear) as street fashion and the music they listen to, notably drill music."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "British",
                                            "Multicultural-London-English",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "660863ec-2607-41a2-b78e-8f1f0160e060",
                                                "sense_id": "1d0f6589-077a-31b8-b35d-b63ec92129c8",
                                                "text": "And officers’ definition of ‘roadman’ could prove to be controversial. They described the term as a ‘teenager who involves themselves in smoking weed, no education, puffa jacket and man bag, acts hard on a bike’."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f70bf22d-8540-45ff-92a2-1d9127246a40",
                                                "sense_id": "1d0f6589-077a-31b8-b35d-b63ec92129c8",
                                                "text": "The roadman look is very working-class (although it can be made to appear high-end), and features key pieces like matching tracksuits, technical jackets (like Nike wind runners or lightweight Stone Island shells) running caps, ‘trainers’ (like any Nike Air Max or a Reebok Classic), bum/shoulder bags, and maybe even a scarf on colder days."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b84ccf18-ef5b-491c-8dff-071843dc2f7e",
